canela (0.1.39) unstable; urgency=low

  * Times: the head of each MIRCO output shows how long its cell ran
    (Ausgabe · laden · 5,8 s); each REPL answer ends with its time, a
    recomputed block with the time of all its inputs; while MIRCO
    computes the title counts the seconds.
  * Compute MIRCO Line computes the block again as one programme: a line
    that binds a name again replaces the old binding (no H6020), the
    lines after it get new answers.
  * A message of the compiler under a REPL input is one short line.
  * Markdown > HTML > Markdown keeps the whole info line of a code block
    (the name of a MIRCO cell, the time of an output).

 -- Heiko Zimmermann  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:55:51 +0100

canela (0.1.38) unstable; urgency=low

  * Compute MIRCO REPL Again gives all inputs to MIRCO as one programme
    (tools/mirco-repl batch): the 16 inputs of the example take 4 s
    instead of 33 to 41 s; with an older MIRCO they are computed one by
    one as before.
  * The results of MIRCO cells and REPL inputs are taken in within
    50 ms of their end, not at the next second.

